@@ -51,3 +51,35 @@
 	  This table can provide power data and capacity to someone who
 	  need it.
 	  If unsure, say Y.
+
+config MAIC_CPU_OC
+	bool "MAIC: MT8167 CPU overclock OPPs (1400 MHz @ 1.325 V, 1500 MHz @ 1.35 V)"
+	depends on MACH_MT8167 && CPU_FREQ
+	default n
+	help
+	  Adds two operating points above the stock 1300 MHz top OPP of the
+	  MT8167 (Cortex-A35) on the default/1.3G efuse bin. The stock DTB is
+	  not modified. Voltages stay at or below the buck_vproc DT maximum of
+	  1350 mV. PTP/EEM does not adjust the new OPPs (its model is calibrated
+	  at 1300 MHz), so they run at the fixed voltages above.
+
+	  The new OPPs are DORMANT at boot: the cpufreq policy maximum starts
+	  at 1300 MHz, so a kernel built with this option behaves like stock
+	  until userspace raises scaling_max_freq to 1400000 or 1500000.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
+
+config MAIC_GPU_OC
+	bool "MAIC: MT8167 GPU 494 MHz OPP (vcore raised to 1.25 V at that OPP)"
+	depends on MACH_MT8167
+	default n
+	help
+	  Selects the vendor "500M" GE8300 table (494 MHz @ 1.25 V, then the
+	  stock 403/299/253.5 MHz @ 1.15 V) on units that efuse/DT into the
+	  400M table, and enables the regulator call for the GPU supply, which
+	  on this board is MT6392 buck_vcore -- the whole SoC's digital rail.
+	  vcore is clamped to 1150..1250 mV and only rises while the GPU is at
+	  494 MHz. Verified before writing this: eMMC/SD clocks (msdc0/1 on
+	  mainpll_d8, msdc2 on univpll_d6) do not derive from MMPLL.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
