+	 * MAIC: the vendor compiled this out, so the GPU table voltages were
+	 * never applied. With the 494 MHz OPP enabled vcore must rise to
+	 * 1.25 V for that OPP. vcore is the shared SoC digital rail: clamp it
+	 * to [1150, 1250] mV so this can never undervolt the SoC below the
